  "decontamination_notes": "Real fix from agronholm/anyio PR #1218, merged 2026-07-11, after model training cutoffs, so the specific fix is novel. Repo sliced at the PR's base commit 44713f3 (src/anyio + pyproject.toml + MIT LICENSE). Runs in the per-task image vulcanbench/sandbox:anyio-1191 (anyio's runtime deps + trio preinstalled, anyio itself imported from the workspace via PYTHONPATH=src). The bug: on the trio backend, CapacityLimiter.acquire_nowait / acquire_on_behalf_of_nowait leaked trio.WouldBlock instead of anyio.WouldBlock when the limiter was full. Hidden tests drive the public anyio API on the trio backend via anyio.run(backend='trio') and assert anyio.WouldBlock is raised; never internal backend state.",
